Aerie-Purpose: Put the "Links open" row in the Sidebar section of Settings, let the settings page write its pref, and give the page its strings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private (prefs_util.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #141. The row, settings-aerie-links-open-row, is a Lit element in the overlay
(chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/aerie_links_open_row.*): a settings-dropdown-menu on the
profile pref aerie.tabs.links_open ("new-tab", the default, or "in-place"), added to the settings_private
allowlist here as a string literal; a test compares it with aerie_tab_model::kLinksOpen. It is the global value
that a folder's "Links open" inherits, and it takes effect without a restart. Its strings are in the overlay's
aerie_sidebar_strings.grdp, which patches/sidebar/0022 includes in generated_resources.grd; this patch hands
them to the page. The element sits in the "Sidebar" section, under the archive rows of patches/sidebar/0049.

